---
title: Flagged clipboard items and MCP reads
date: '2026-09-24'
tags:
  - changed
  - fixed
summary: Flagged items are omitted from Clipwell MCP recent/search results and refused by MCP direct-text reads; trusted local REST picker clients retain access.
---
<script>
  import ThemedShot from '$lib/components/changelog/ThemedShot.svelte';
  import ThemedClip from '$lib/components/changelog/ThemedClip.svelte';
</script>

This dated [source update](https://github.com/aylith-labs/clipwell/commit/d14aa3abc02139b1d68c77ab4f33adf22bd4a3f2)
narrows what Clipwell's MCP tools can read. Recent items and search omit a
flagged row, including an alias match; direct text reads refuse it. The local
REST view remains available to trusted picker clients so the item can still be
managed. This does not secure every local API caller or an unflagged item.

## Source-run web-picker study · 2026-09-25

These paired captures come from the **actual browser-served `/app` web picker**
and .NET daemon, using seven fictional rows in an isolated database with
clipboard watching disabled. They do not depict the native Windows picker or
any real clipboard contents. One fictional row was marked sensitive through
the product API; the picker shows it masked. The poster's MCP explanation is
source-backed, not a fabricated MCP response.

